1319:- FINDINGS (all verified against the raw document, each would have been a silent wrong-source derivation): the request envelope sentence exists three times (7.5-style, 7.8, 7.9) and the capability-value sentence twice (Provider Probe 7.4 vs Session Adapter Probe 7.8) — selection is by a structural fragment only the Session Adapter sentence carries, and the parse still covers the whole sentence; member sentences contain digit-period-digit abbreviations (`Section 7.5`, `Structured Error 1.1`), so the sentence scanner skips those; unions use three pipe encodings (`\|` in the operation table, raw `|` in prose, `&#124;` in the manifest table); the manifest table pairs members per row (`schema`/`schema_version` etc.), so the first cell contributes every bare snake_case span; the `probe` row name recurs in four tables, so row unions are windowed to the 7.8 registry table; fidelity profiles come from the `projection-plan` operation row (4 values — the 13.14 `Profiles are` sentence lists 5 including `archive_only`, which is a strategy there, never a profile).
1349:- EVIDENCE: battery 30 applied / 30 killed / 0 survivors (16 narrowing incl N13–N16, 10 arm-deletion, 2 census-only, 2 audit-only; NOT_APPLIED + COMPILE_FAIL distinct); `go test ./...` 24/24 green, `-race` green in 4 groups (all 24 pkgs), vet + GOOS=windows vet/build + gofmt clean, tracecheck 60/98, sessrepo cover 87.2%. Tree `93d4a106fd15cdb335539c2612d3ed84d70f919a` (detached-index write-tree over README + 7 sessrepo files). Outcome + battery log attached as `TASK-260830-wbpf1v_outcome-rev3.md` / `TASK-260830-wbpf1v_mutation-battery-rev3.log`.
